<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lorelei (Franz Liszt)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">musical setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">La Loreley (Guillaume Apollinaire, in Alcools)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">poem on the same theme</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 14, third movement (Dmitri Shostakovich)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting of Apollinaire's poem</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Our Mother the Mountain (Townes Van Zandt)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969</span><span class="sg-chain-h">reference in the title track</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Editions of You (Roxy Music)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1973</span><span class="sg-chain-h">reference</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lorelei (The Pogues)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1989</span><span class="sg-chain-h">song on the theme</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">When Mermaids Cry (Eagle-Eye Cherry)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1998</span><span class="sg-chain-h">reference</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lorelei (David Gray)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2002</span><span class="sg-chain-h">song on the theme</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Loreley (Blackmore's Night, Ghost of a Rose)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2004</span><span class="sg-chain-h">song on the theme</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lorelei (Fischer-Z, This Is My Universe)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2015</span><span class="sg-chain-h">song on the theme</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Eyrie (Ne Obliviscaris, Urn)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2017</span><span class="sg-chain-h">song on the theme</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Zu Bacharach am Rheine (Clemens Brentano)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1801</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Heine adapted its theme</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Myth of Echo (Ovid)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">ancient</span><span class="sg-chain-h">inspiration for Brentano's ballad</span></li></ul></section>
